- [will_said] SENTRON AGES - RULINGS (Will, EE 8): the Age field is 42 bits ('We'll use 42 bits, naturally') - Age = floor(seconds into epoch x 2^42 / 420), range 0 to 4,398,046,511,103; ages are less accurate than epochs (time sync is bad at this grain; 1 ms skew is ~10.47M ages; an Age is local/nominal, the epoch is the shared coordinate). Coarse ages for now: a 16-bit space (fine >> 26, ~6.41 ms per tick), to be used for the register going forward and added to libphext-rs. Naming (Will): 'we're calling the ages Sentron Ages next to Exocortical Epochs' - one EE = 2^42 fine or 65,536 coarse Sentron Ages.

