- [verified] EXO GATE G1 FAILED ON ITS EXIT CONDITION (EE ~33; record ~/workspace/exo-integration/G1-REPORT.md): MLX v0.32.4 built from source on ni-knight (-march=native, system OpenBLAS/LAPACK, separate ~/g1-venv; ~/exo and exo.service untouched): dense matmul 4096^3 rose 6.9 -> 832.4 GFLOP/s (~121x; the wheel's libmlx links bundled reference BLAS with 0 AVX-512 instructions vs 83,200 in the source build). Generation did not move: 4-bit Llama-3.2-1B generate still DNF in 900 s, bf16 control 1.184 t/s (vs 1.409 in Stage 1). Measured root cause: MLX x86 quantized_matmul is a generic fallback - 2.5 GFLOP/s, single-threaded, flat across batch sizes - and decode pins one core. Next candidate named G1b: AVX-512 threaded quantized-matmul kernel work in MLX's CPU backend (days-scale). PENDING Will's decision: commission G1b, or take the correctness-first bf16 serve (~1.2 t/s class) and let speed wait; posed to Will 2026-11-22, no ruling recorded at flush time.

