- [verified] G1b PASSES BOTH GATES (report on disk is the record: ~/workspace/exo-integration/G1B-REPORT.md): root cause from MLX v0.32.4 source - the CPU SIMD layer has NO x86 vector implementation (simd max_size == 1, so the SIMD qmm dispatch is never selected; stock path is scalar) and no intra-op thread pool in the quantized path. Fix: one file, mlx/backend/cpu/quantized.cpp - AVX-512 dequantize+FMA kernel plus a small persistent thread pool, dispatched only for transposed affine bits 4/8 with a runtime AVX-512 check; installed into ~/g1-venv on ni-knight only. Numbers: quantized_matmul bits=4 about 40x (2.45 to 98.3 GFLOP/s class); 4-bit Llama-3.2-1B generate went from DNF in 900 s to completing at 11.64 tok/s; bf16 control 1.184 to 1.367 t/s, no regression. Correctness: 37-case battery vs float64 - G1b is MORE accurate than stock in all 37 cases. GPU finding (Will 07:49 steering): MLX cannot address the 780M on this platform - no ROCm/HIP backend in the v0.32.4 tree; the exo path is CPU by construction and fleet GPU leverage lives in the llama.cpp/HIP path. PENDING: G1b R9 APU spot-check (report R9 section left a placeholder; follow-up worker dispatched, no result yet) and the llama.cpp update + Inkling optimization pass (still running; deliverable owed at ~/workspace/exo-integration/INKLING-PERF.md).

